    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227-a1">

                <pb facs="0984" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg834"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Chargé
                        McCreery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>: As a result of your note,
                    dated January 29 last, I have the honor to transmit to you herewith copy of a
                    communication I have received from the department of government, stating that it
                    is not possible to <pb facs="0985" n="835" xml:id="pg835"/> waive the requisite
                    of consular visa, under the basis of mutual interests in the commercial
                    relations between Mexico and the United States, because said requisite is
                    ordered by articles 37 of the Sanitary Code and 67 of the General Customs
                    Regulations.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
